  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance and Capacity Building for the Government of Ukraine - Developing and Implementing Interim Reparative Measures and Reparations for Survivors of Conflict-Related Sexual Violence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this intervention, IOM intends to endow the Government of Ukraine with context-specific tools, knowledge, and a strategy to develop and implement inclusive, timely, and effective policies and legal frameworks that ensure the provision of reparations to survivors of conflict-related sexual violence and other conflict-affected people. To this end, IOM and its partners will provide expert advice, technical assistance and policy support to the Government to adopt a comprehensive reparations policy and legislation for victims of the war. The intervention focuses on the fifth pillar defined in the Implementation Plan of the Cooperation Framework between the UN and the Government of Ukraine.</narrative>
  </description>
